bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_inline_item_layoutunit_ceil_pen_2026-11-28, 0, "Chrome 159 stores an inline item's width as LayoutUnit::FromFloatCeil of its exact advance sum (1/64 px) and starts the next item there: <code>audio</code> at 16 px DejaVu Sans Mono is 48.1640625 px exact and 48.171875 in Chrome, <code>a</code> 9.6328125 and 9.640625, <code>button</code> 57.796875 in both. The one-run branch of inline_item_width_err_milli returns the exact width, so the next run's pen origin is 1/128 px short whenever the item is an odd number of 1/128 px wide, and a glyph one step under a quarter tie takes the lower LCD phase: a whole glyph 0.25 px left, 60 to 100 mismatching px. Single-glyph phase misses left on the 1x catalog: html 3, forms-media 4, animation 1."
    web_render_inline_item_layoutunit_ceil_pen_2026-11-28, 1, "Not a one-line ceil. (1) resolved_font_width_milli is a sum of milli-rounded advances (six mono glyphs give 57.798, not 57.796875), so a ceil steps button up a LayoutUnit: _text_pen_milli must return exact unit sums first. (2) The edge-space branches ceil the space apart from the text; Chrome ceils the item once, and the lead-space item (space + text) once. (3) Trial with (1) and a 0.6 milli slack ceil in the one-run branch only: 1x html 0.29 -> 0.28, css-layout 0.40 -> 0.37, forms-media 0.34 -> 0.33, animation 0.34 -> 0.32, but overview 0.16 -> 0.19 (Paragraph with <strong>..</strong>, <em>..</em>, <code>: three new glyphs). Every branch has to follow the rule before any of it lands."
    web_render_inline_item_layoutunit_ceil_pen_2026-11-28, 2, "Acceptance probe: <ul style=margin:0;padding:0 0 0 30px><li><code>button|audio|a|kbd</code> — partial|renderable; values=element; owner=simple_web_html_layout, 16 px sans-serif #172033 on white, mismatching px per line against Chrome 159 (a line without a phase miss is about 200): upstream 8b2da8a67a1 202 212 260 260 (934); exact pens + snapped lead 450 212 197 193 (1052); exact pens + exact lead (landed) 202 270 260 318 (1050). The item ceil plus the exact lead should give about 200 on all four."

